WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:19.312
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:19.582 --> 00:20.875
I'm not a spy.

3
00:21.376 --> 00:23.837
I'm not an international student either.

4
00:23.920 --> 00:24.796
Sir, I…

5
00:26.339 --> 00:27.882
I've never even been to college.

6
00:27.966 --> 00:29.175
I swear.

7
00:30.385 --> 00:33.179
I think there was a misunderstanding. I'm sorry.

8
00:44.274 --> 00:46.025
You're not Korean, are you?

9
00:55.451 --> 00:56.327
Eat.

10
00:56.411 --> 00:57.745
Thank you.

11
01:01.791 --> 01:05.920
I crossed over from the North and work here.

12
01:08.256 --> 01:09.507
They said if I work here,

13
01:11.050 --> 01:15.221
they'll eventually issue me a resident registration card.

14
01:17.724 --> 01:18.558
Right.

15
01:27.317 --> 01:29.194
Any interest in working with us?

16
01:36.910 --> 01:38.369
Hey, Seo Hyun-tae.

17
01:38.453 --> 01:39.537
Yes?

18
01:40.121 --> 01:41.247
Where are you from?

19
01:45.126 --> 01:46.252
Look.

20
01:47.295 --> 01:49.964
Whether it's North Korea, China, or the Soviet Union,

21
01:51.007 --> 01:52.759
you've nowhere to return to, do you?

22
01:59.849 --> 02:01.100
Don't be afraid.

23
02:03.144 --> 02:04.312
Don't be afraid.

24
03:21.014 --> 03:22.807
THE BLUE ROAD

25
03:46.622 --> 03:48.124
Mommy, look.

26
04:00.511 --> 04:01.763
Inose.

27
04:02.764 --> 04:04.974
You left us so suddenly.

28
04:05.058 --> 04:06.726
I still can't believe it.

29
04:07.769 --> 04:13.149
We will never forget the deep sorrow and regret

30
04:13.775 --> 04:16.027
of losing a precious comrade.

31
04:17.153 --> 04:18.905
All of us in the police department…

32
04:18.988 --> 04:22.450
How dare that Korean detective show his face here?

33
04:22.533 --> 04:25.411
I hear the drug trafficking charges against him were dropped.

34
04:25.495 --> 04:29.082
Doesn't he realize whose fault it is that Inose's dead?

35
04:29.165 --> 04:30.416
Keep it down.

36
04:31.000 --> 04:33.294
Please rest in peace.

37
04:52.355 --> 04:53.231
Excuse me.

38
04:54.107 --> 04:54.941
Just a moment.

39
05:02.115 --> 05:03.116
You're

40
05:03.866 --> 05:04.992
Mr. Kim Seok?

41
05:05.868 --> 05:06.702
Yes.

42
05:09.539 --> 05:11.082
About what happened to Inose…

43
05:12.834 --> 05:14.502
I am truly sorry.

44
05:20.133 --> 05:21.843
Of course you should be.

45
05:24.512 --> 05:27.640
How am I supposed to afford Rumi's child support now?

46
05:31.769 --> 05:34.730
What? Do you think I'm being too much?

47
05:35.565 --> 05:37.692
-Even toward an ex-husband? -No.

48
05:39.277 --> 05:40.736
I don't think that at all.

49
05:42.572 --> 05:45.491
I'm sure Inose is sorry as well.

50
05:46.033 --> 05:48.453
Mister, is your face okay?

51
05:52.832 --> 05:53.916
It's fine.

52
05:54.834 --> 05:57.086
Korea one day, Hong Kong the next…

53
05:57.670 --> 05:59.922
Who did he think he was, Superman?

54
06:01.132 --> 06:02.842
I don't know if it was for you

55
06:04.469 --> 06:07.096
or because of some sense of duty as a police officer…

56
06:13.186 --> 06:16.022
But whatever it was, being a cop is an awful job.

57
06:20.026 --> 06:21.068
Lastly…

58
06:30.536 --> 06:32.705
he wanted me to give this to you.

59
07:30.054 --> 07:33.849
OLD CITY

60
08:48.549 --> 08:50.551
Dandelion Village?

61
08:54.013 --> 08:56.891
Are you going there to kill somebody? For revenge?

62
08:58.893 --> 09:00.227
You Japanese? Chinese?

63
09:00.895 --> 09:02.438
I said he's Korean.

64
09:03.981 --> 09:05.107
Korean?

65
09:07.151 --> 09:08.319
Anastasia!

66
09:13.574 --> 09:15.951
Give him a ride to Dandelion Village.

67
09:16.911 --> 09:18.746
Your mom is a Koryo-saram, right?

68
09:20.873 --> 09:22.708
Not the mom who raised me.

69
09:22.792 --> 09:24.543
The one who gave birth to me.

70
09:26.420 --> 09:27.505
Either way.

71
09:28.005 --> 09:29.799
You speak their language, right?

72
09:45.439 --> 09:46.273
Follow me.

73
09:59.161 --> 10:00.955
Why are you looking at me like that?

74
10:02.331 --> 10:04.458
You just look like someone I know.

75
10:07.461 --> 10:09.004
Your Korean…

76
10:10.297 --> 10:11.799
Did you learn it from somewhere?

77
10:15.803 --> 10:17.138
From Mama.

78
10:19.098 --> 10:20.641
Mama told me

79
10:21.934 --> 10:23.561
that we need to return someday.

80
10:24.729 --> 10:28.441
And that when we do, we can't not know our own language.

81
10:29.608 --> 10:31.277
You intend to go back to Korea?

82
10:32.820 --> 10:33.988
Mama died.

83
10:35.740 --> 10:36.907
So, no, I'm not.

84
10:37.908 --> 10:39.535
That isn't my country.

85
10:40.494 --> 10:42.121
We have no country of our own.

86
10:58.179 --> 11:00.097
A friend from the Blue Road.

87
11:05.352 --> 11:07.021
The Blue Road.

88
11:09.982 --> 11:11.317
In the Koryo language…

89
11:14.111 --> 11:15.237
The Blue Road.

90
11:19.950 --> 11:22.912
Our people, the people of Joseon,

91
11:24.330 --> 11:25.664
were driven here

92
11:26.499 --> 11:27.500
from Joseon.

93
11:29.376 --> 11:31.003
They didn't want to come,

94
11:31.921 --> 11:33.881
but they had no choice.

95
11:34.715 --> 11:36.342
They embraced the cold and endured.

96
11:37.760 --> 11:39.053
And on the long walk over…

97
11:41.263 --> 11:42.473
they cried.

98
11:43.849 --> 11:45.226
Their tears just fell.

99
11:48.687 --> 11:50.689
That's why it's called the Blue Road.

100
11:52.608 --> 11:54.443
Because tears are blue…

101
11:57.404 --> 11:58.614
or so they say.

102
12:08.040 --> 12:09.375
The Blue Road.

103
12:27.935 --> 12:31.021
We still have three hours to go until we reach Dandelion Village.

104
12:31.522 --> 12:35.192
But no one lives there anymore. There isn't even a place to sleep.

105
12:36.527 --> 12:38.195
Sleep here tonight.

106
12:44.285 --> 12:45.619
All you'll find there now

107
12:46.787 --> 12:48.622
are graves and gangs.

108
12:52.960 --> 12:54.587
That's why I'm going there.

109
13:52.353 --> 13:53.395
Forgive me.

110
14:04.073 --> 14:05.074
Stop!

111
14:55.082 --> 14:56.208
Hey.

112
15:02.131 --> 15:03.173
What?

113
15:04.341 --> 15:07.386
Didn't expect me to pull a Jesus and rise from the dead?

114
15:10.222 --> 15:14.226
INOSE HIROSHI ABDOMINAL GSW, NON-LIFE-THREATENING

115
15:16.311 --> 15:19.398
Inose? Is it really you?

116
15:19.481 --> 15:21.984
Yes, it's me.

117
15:23.736 --> 15:26.488
You're Chief Shimizu of Investigations Division 1.

118
15:26.989 --> 15:30.868
After three years of missed promotions, you drank your sorrows away at my place,

119
15:30.951 --> 15:33.328
only to get kicked out for puking everywhere.

120
15:36.331 --> 15:37.916
It really is you.

121
15:38.000 --> 15:41.003
There's no time to explain. I'm counting on you, Chief.

122
15:41.086 --> 15:42.629
I want to catch Ito.

123
15:44.673 --> 15:46.300
How can I help?

124
15:50.721 --> 15:51.847
Hey, what the heck?

125
15:51.930 --> 15:54.058
Police! Back up.

126
15:54.141 --> 15:57.061
What? Do you even have a warrant?

127
15:57.144 --> 15:59.104
What are you doing, crashing our shoot?

128
16:00.773 --> 16:03.650
After all the complaints about defamation and spreading lies,

129
16:03.734 --> 16:05.861
you're asking for a warrant, are you?

130
16:05.944 --> 16:07.905
I can absolutely bring one if you want.

131
16:07.988 --> 16:10.240
No, wait. That's not what I meant.

132
16:10.324 --> 16:13.452
Since that's not what you meant,

133
16:13.535 --> 16:15.788
let us use your show.

134
16:15.871 --> 16:20.042
Such a tragic death in the line of duty!

135
16:22.336 --> 16:24.588
And on top of that,

136
16:25.089 --> 16:29.259
the Korean detective who worked the case with him was so shaken

137
16:29.343 --> 16:32.513
that he left the police force for good.

138
16:35.140 --> 16:36.016
In other words,

139
16:36.517 --> 16:40.187
if a rumor circulates that I'm dead and Detective Kim quit the force,

140
16:40.687 --> 16:42.731
Seo Hyun-tae should start moving.

141
16:43.649 --> 16:44.691
Then

142
16:45.234 --> 16:47.111
Speed K will hit the streets again.

143
16:47.194 --> 16:49.404
I don't know if I'm doing the right thing here.

144
16:52.241 --> 16:53.117
Chief.

145
16:54.993 --> 16:56.036
They had this…

146
16:58.831 --> 17:01.959
What the hell is this? We haven't seen this stuff in a while.

147
17:03.460 --> 17:04.336
Hey.

148
17:05.129 --> 17:06.672
Where did you get this?

149
17:07.172 --> 17:09.883
Security service will then trace it back to the source.

150
17:15.347 --> 17:17.933
There should be a hospital three kilometers from here.

151
17:18.433 --> 17:19.685
And the police.

152
17:20.769 --> 17:21.854
Step on it.

153
17:23.814 --> 17:25.732
Go!

154
17:34.741 --> 17:36.702
Ito must have caught on.

155
17:39.413 --> 17:40.581
Let's hurry.

156
17:52.551 --> 17:53.969
Please spare me.

157
18:08.400 --> 18:10.319
Yeah. She looks like her.

158
18:18.076 --> 18:19.328
I'm sorry.

159
18:20.287 --> 18:21.455
Are you okay?

160
18:23.415 --> 18:24.875
Are you hurt?

161
18:28.795 --> 18:29.880
Thank goodness.

162
18:35.385 --> 18:38.388
It could be dangerous, so don't go back the way we came.

163
18:40.515 --> 18:42.434
And if you ever come to Korea…

164
18:44.394 --> 18:45.938
contact me here.

165
18:47.648 --> 18:54.196
SEOUL METROPOLITAN POLICE AGENCY INSPECTOR KIM SEOK

166
18:54.863 --> 18:55.781
Let's go.

167
19:25.852 --> 19:28.855
We're here on an Interpol operation to catch the culprit.

168
19:31.733 --> 19:32.943
You mustn't kill him.

169
19:35.487 --> 19:37.197
No matter what the bastard does,

170
19:38.865 --> 19:40.450
don't forget your duty as a cop.

171
19:58.719 --> 20:00.262
Kim Seok!

172
20:01.722 --> 20:03.765
You're a cop!

173
20:09.938 --> 20:11.857
I haven't forgotten.

174
20:32.294 --> 20:34.171
DANDELION CEMETERY

175
21:10.290 --> 21:13.752
You sure came a long way.

176
21:20.467 --> 21:21.468
Children.

177
21:30.268 --> 21:31.978
Nice to meet you.

178
21:41.488 --> 21:42.489
Igor.

179
21:43.198 --> 21:44.366
Makoto.

180
21:44.449 --> 21:45.450
Hyun-tae.

181
21:47.411 --> 21:49.621
All three are my names.

182
21:54.459 --> 21:56.002
Hundreds of our compatriots

183
21:57.754 --> 21:59.673
died wretched deaths here.

184
22:01.925 --> 22:03.844
My father and my grandfather

185
22:05.095 --> 22:07.889
were dragged all the way here during the Japanese occupation,

186
22:09.599 --> 22:11.351
taken from their homeland for no reason.

187
22:12.394 --> 22:14.146
But I survived.

188
22:16.356 --> 22:17.524
Like a dandelion.

189
22:24.531 --> 22:25.490
So?

190
22:27.325 --> 22:30.245
Are you saying that makes you a victim who deserves salvation?

191
22:31.621 --> 22:34.040
A victim who produces drugs in a place like this?

192
22:36.877 --> 22:37.836
Let's go inside.

193
23:01.943 --> 23:03.069
Hey, Ito.

194
23:04.654 --> 23:06.156
As of now, you're under arrest.

195
23:06.865 --> 23:10.160
You're charged with aggravated murder, solicitation, abandoning human--

196
23:10.243 --> 23:11.495
Didn't you come here…

197
23:13.705 --> 23:15.957
to hear the rest of Arabian Nights?

198
23:21.713 --> 23:24.799
I've already come to my own conclusions, so don't worry.

199
23:29.721 --> 23:32.891
Whatever Hong Du-yeong was, it has nothing to do with me now, so--

200
23:32.974 --> 23:35.310
Why are you so obsessed with Hong Du-yeong?

201
23:36.728 --> 23:38.313
It's not like he was your father.

202
23:39.523 --> 23:40.398
Then again,

203
23:41.233 --> 23:45.278
Du-yeong did look out for you and your mom until the very end.

204
23:50.534 --> 23:52.702
MUNHWA THEATER SCHEDULED FOR DEMOLITION

205
23:52.786 --> 23:55.038
I heard the director retired and went to Japan

206
23:55.539 --> 23:58.250
and that you were living in Gunsan.

207
23:58.333 --> 23:59.584
Yeah.

208
24:00.544 --> 24:02.754
The director was granted some state land.

209
24:04.047 --> 24:06.424
He's going to build some pharmaceutical plant there.

210
24:07.384 --> 24:11.388
It's the family business, but if he were to build it in Japan, well…

211
24:12.264 --> 24:14.099
People would raise hell about pollution.

212
24:21.356 --> 24:22.857
Shunsuke. Go play outside.

213
24:22.941 --> 24:24.693
RESIDENT REGISTRATION CARD SEO HYUN-TAE

214
24:28.363 --> 24:30.198
Du-yeong, let's go in.

215
24:49.009 --> 24:50.385
He's the director's son.

216
24:51.970 --> 24:53.430
I'm looking after him.

217
24:55.307 --> 24:56.891
I couldn't leave him alone.

218
25:12.073 --> 25:15.452
Did they tell you to kill me in exchange for an ID card?

219
25:19.539 --> 25:21.499
If you know, why are you so calm?

220
25:25.545 --> 25:27.130
I finally get it.

221
25:28.965 --> 25:31.009
That the things we did

222
25:32.427 --> 25:34.471
are unforgivable.

223
25:52.280 --> 25:53.239
What did you say?

224
25:58.703 --> 26:02.874
I've been so happy lately that I realize it all the more.

225
26:04.668 --> 26:06.920
That forgiveness

226
26:08.463 --> 26:09.881
is a luxury for us.

227
26:13.134 --> 26:14.678
You're so happy?

228
26:29.109 --> 26:30.777
You've got to be kidding me.

229
26:53.550 --> 26:54.676
Then die.

230
26:58.179 --> 26:59.055
Hey.

231
26:59.556 --> 27:00.640
Who

232
27:01.599 --> 27:02.726
the hell

233
27:04.227 --> 27:06.771
do we need forgiveness from?

234
27:09.482 --> 27:10.984
I'm begging you.

235
27:12.068 --> 27:17.115
Don't hurt the kid or his mom.

236
27:19.451 --> 27:20.994
Die, you bastard.

237
27:21.578 --> 27:22.412
Die.

238
28:06.623 --> 28:07.749
It's Emiri.

239
28:14.547 --> 28:15.548
So?

240
28:17.217 --> 28:18.593
So what?

241
28:20.845 --> 28:24.974
I only came here to arrest a moron who willingly confessed to killing people.

242
28:27.185 --> 28:28.353
Get up now.

243
28:29.187 --> 28:31.940
You believe your father went missing, don't you?

244
28:35.443 --> 28:36.778
What did you just say?

245
28:38.404 --> 28:39.864
-Enough. -Just a second.

246
28:40.657 --> 28:41.741
Arrest him.

247
28:43.409 --> 28:44.702
Arrest him!

248
28:47.121 --> 28:49.916
Why? What are you afraid of?

249
28:59.551 --> 29:00.385
Go on.

250
29:15.942 --> 29:17.735
Before we retired…

251
29:19.028 --> 29:20.572
RESIDENT REGISTRATION CARD HONG DU-YEONG

252
29:20.655 --> 29:21.698
Look at this.

253
29:25.535 --> 29:26.911
I'm a Korean citizen now.

254
29:28.496 --> 29:30.957
Wait, how did this happen?

255
29:31.624 --> 29:33.126
When did they issue you this?

256
29:33.209 --> 29:36.170
Come on. You'll get yours soon enough.

257
29:38.172 --> 29:40.466
Word is the Print Shop will be disbanded.

258
29:41.718 --> 29:43.052
It's being disbanded?

259
29:45.972 --> 29:50.018
With the Olympics coming up and all those foreigners flying in,

260
29:50.101 --> 29:51.769
they'll want to erase scum like us.

261
29:51.853 --> 29:54.397
And what about me? What about my ID?

262
29:54.480 --> 29:55.815
You worry too much.

263
29:56.816 --> 29:58.192
I'm sure they'll give you one.

264
29:59.569 --> 30:02.113
You know far too many secrets.

265
30:03.823 --> 30:05.408
Just wait a little longer.

266
30:09.203 --> 30:10.914
So, if they disband the Print Shop,

267
30:11.998 --> 30:13.291
what will you do?

268
30:14.959 --> 30:17.503
I have something in mind.

269
30:21.591 --> 30:23.176
This woman. Pretty, isn't she?

270
30:28.348 --> 30:29.641
What is this?

271
30:36.147 --> 30:36.981
I found this

272
30:38.107 --> 30:40.234
inside his wallet back then.

273
30:43.863 --> 30:47.033
I'm thinking of paying his home a visit.

274
30:49.786 --> 30:52.038
Imagine how lonely she must be.

275
30:52.747 --> 30:54.415
I feel awful.

276
30:55.416 --> 30:58.336
And who knows? Maybe we'll end up living together.

277
31:01.673 --> 31:03.508
Life has to go on.

278
31:06.803 --> 31:08.054
Are you crazy?

279
31:08.805 --> 31:09.639
What?

280
31:11.140 --> 31:12.850
Are you out of your mind?

281
31:16.646 --> 31:18.898
Have we ever been in our right minds?

282
31:22.694 --> 31:23.861
Missing?

283
31:25.780 --> 31:28.074
Hong Du-yeong buried your father in the hills

284
31:28.741 --> 31:30.952
so that he would never be found.

285
31:33.621 --> 31:34.539
What do you think?

286
31:35.540 --> 31:36.541
Isn't he something?

287
31:40.253 --> 31:41.838
And he called himself human.

288
31:45.091 --> 31:46.843
All because he thought she was pretty…

289
31:49.178 --> 31:51.931
The woman in a photo, found in the wallet of a man we killed.

290
31:56.894 --> 31:58.104
Kim Seok!

291
31:58.187 --> 32:00.440
-He actually went to see you. -Say one more word.

292
32:00.523 --> 32:02.316
He's playing you! Kim Seok, stop!

293
32:02.400 --> 32:03.651
He deserved to die.

294
32:05.987 --> 32:07.155
Hey, Kim.

295
32:07.238 --> 32:08.406
Kim Seok!

296
32:08.489 --> 32:10.366
Look at me when you're talking to me.

297
32:11.909 --> 32:13.161
Can't bear to look at me?

298
32:13.244 --> 32:14.328
Shut up.

299
32:15.204 --> 32:16.205
Enough!

300
32:16.289 --> 32:17.623
Inose.

301
32:32.764 --> 32:34.390
Don't worry. He won't die just yet.

302
32:44.192 --> 32:46.069
This is probably more pressing for you.

303
32:52.075 --> 32:53.242
What are you doing?

304
32:58.372 --> 32:59.916
Of course, your mom won't know.

305
33:07.173 --> 33:08.633
Ready and waiting, sir.

306
33:17.475 --> 33:19.811
Who are you?

307
33:21.145 --> 33:24.107
Are you really Seok's friend?

308
33:24.732 --> 33:25.775
Seok.

309
33:26.567 --> 33:28.528
Seok, I'm scared.

310
33:32.156 --> 33:34.117
Du-yeong.

311
33:35.785 --> 33:40.414
Du-yeong, where are you? Where did you go?

312
33:40.498 --> 33:41.624
Stand by for a moment.

313
33:43.459 --> 33:44.335
Well?

314
33:46.254 --> 33:48.881
Hong Du-yeong, the man she lived with like a new husband,

315
33:50.633 --> 33:52.927
is actually a subhuman bastard,

316
33:54.637 --> 33:57.849
who not only killed her husband but even took his place.

317
33:59.600 --> 34:00.852
Can I tell her that?

318
34:05.481 --> 34:07.233
I don't know if she can handle it.

319
34:08.568 --> 34:10.820
The old lady's in poor health as it is.

320
34:14.365 --> 34:15.366
Well?

321
34:17.618 --> 34:19.036
Should I tell her or not?

322
34:26.669 --> 34:27.837
I'll back off.

323
34:28.337 --> 34:29.338
Satisfied?

324
34:30.339 --> 34:32.884
I was wrong, Seo Hyun-tae.

325
34:34.719 --> 34:35.970
So just stop now.

326
34:46.147 --> 34:47.565
What should…

327
34:50.610 --> 34:51.903
I do?

328
34:56.741 --> 35:00.077
I'm sorry. Forgive me.

329
35:01.787 --> 35:03.539
I'm sorry.

330
35:09.295 --> 35:10.671
Mu-seong, what's going on?

331
35:14.717 --> 35:15.927
What's going on, Mu-seong?

332
35:16.677 --> 35:18.346
Mu-seong, what's going on?!

333
35:22.767 --> 35:25.353
Let's not make a scene, okay?

334
35:25.436 --> 35:26.270
Mu-seong!

335
35:34.153 --> 35:35.196
It's all right.

336
35:36.614 --> 35:38.282
You're all right, ma'am.

337
35:42.495 --> 35:43.579
Mr. Kim Seok.

338
35:46.123 --> 35:47.250
Your mother is safe.

339
36:06.102 --> 36:07.353
I'll go.

340
36:08.020 --> 36:09.230
I'll go.

341
36:09.730 --> 36:10.898
You stay here.

342
36:55.067 --> 36:56.402
I have to end this.

343
36:57.862 --> 36:58.946
Me.

344
37:30.728 --> 37:33.064
I'm sick of this now. Enough.

345
37:38.944 --> 37:40.363
I'm sick of it.

346
38:03.344 --> 38:04.387
Shoot me.

347
38:05.888 --> 38:07.390
You should shoot me this time.

348
38:11.477 --> 38:14.188
You're afraid right now, aren't you?

349
38:19.068 --> 38:19.902
No.

350
38:21.487 --> 38:22.446
I'm not afraid.

351
38:27.743 --> 38:28.619
Kim Seok!

352
38:33.707 --> 38:34.625
What are you doing?!

353
38:40.673 --> 38:41.549
Stop it!

354
38:42.925 --> 38:44.093
Stop it!

355
38:52.643 --> 38:55.563
We're detectives. We're the police!

356
38:57.731 --> 38:59.608
We arrest people, bring them to justice.

357
39:00.776 --> 39:02.862
That's what we do!

358
39:04.321 --> 39:05.322
Kim Seok.

359
39:06.282 --> 39:07.700
Kim Seok!

360
39:08.367 --> 39:09.743
You're afraid.

361
39:11.370 --> 39:13.205
You're afraid right now.

362
39:16.000 --> 39:16.834
Kim Seok!

363
39:16.917 --> 39:17.918
Afraid.

364
39:38.481 --> 39:39.857
Don't be afraid.

365
39:49.658 --> 39:51.035
Don't be afraid.

366
40:36.914 --> 40:39.083
Kim Seok!

367
40:40.209 --> 40:42.211
Kim Seok!

368
40:45.214 --> 40:46.131
It's okay.

369
40:47.591 --> 40:48.509
It's okay.

370
40:50.135 --> 40:51.095
You'll be okay.

371
40:51.178 --> 40:52.972
Kim Seok! You're okay.

372
40:55.683 --> 40:56.517
Kim Seok.

373
40:56.600 --> 40:57.768
Inose.

374
41:00.896 --> 41:01.730
I've…

375
41:04.108 --> 41:06.068
done so much wrong.

376
41:08.696 --> 41:09.822
Still…

377
41:12.825 --> 41:14.368
thanks to you…

378
41:17.663 --> 41:19.748
I think I was able to end things the right way.

379
41:22.876 --> 41:24.253
As a cop.

380
41:26.797 --> 41:27.715
You're okay!

381
41:28.257 --> 41:29.758
Thank you, truly.

382
41:29.842 --> 41:30.718
Kim Seok!

383
42:17.264 --> 42:23.354
THE YEAR 2026

384
42:42.539 --> 42:45.042
Let's move on to our final case.

385
42:55.678 --> 42:58.305
These pictures are difficult to even look at, aren't they?

386
42:59.348 --> 43:03.185
This is a murder case that took place in Japan in 2002.

387
43:05.062 --> 43:07.314
The crime scene is very complex, isn't it?

388
43:07.815 --> 43:09.900
There was even a written message like so.

389
43:12.528 --> 43:15.239
The body was displayed in a very deliberate manner.

390
43:19.451 --> 43:20.619
So

391
43:21.954 --> 43:23.831
who could have devised a method

392
43:24.790 --> 43:25.708
such as this,

393
43:26.625 --> 43:27.501
why,

394
43:28.919 --> 43:30.838
and how did it come about?

395
43:34.717 --> 43:36.969
Was it created by design?

396
43:37.553 --> 43:38.554
Or was it

397
43:39.596 --> 43:41.557
born out of an accident?

398
44:01.869 --> 44:04.788
GOVERNMENT EMPLOYEE ID

399
44:04.872 --> 44:07.541
ANASTASIA KIM NATIONAL POLICE AGENCY

400
44:10.419 --> 44:11.754
You seem to be doing well.

401
44:16.091 --> 44:18.552
It's thanks to you. The both of you.

402
44:29.563 --> 44:31.857
I'm a bit embarrassed to admit this, but…

403
44:32.608 --> 44:34.276
Admit what?

404
44:35.444 --> 44:39.198
Truth is, until yesterday, I'd completely forgotten about today.

405
44:39.698 --> 44:40.783
"Forgotten"?

406
44:43.202 --> 44:44.536
"Forgot"?

407
44:49.374 --> 44:51.752
Still so many words I don't know.

408
45:16.276 --> 45:23.283
GRAVE OF SUPERINTENDENT KIM SEOK

409
45:42.302 --> 45:44.930
It's already been so long.

410
45:50.769 --> 45:51.812
Even so,

411
45:53.564 --> 45:54.898
we must not forget.

412
46:00.904 --> 46:02.197
We don't get to forget…

413
46:07.661 --> 46:09.037
just because it's in the past.

414
46:31.184 --> 46:32.436
I'm sorry.

415
47:23.236 --> 47:24.488
You did good.

416
47:34.790 --> 47:35.999
Good work.

417
48:14.621 --> 48:15.831
I'll always remember.

418
